  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nodes are the spaces where the probability of finding an electron is zero.</p><p>Radial nodes are the nodes that appear along the radius of an atom while angular nodes are the nodes that appear along the plane of an angle.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
